Exactly — **`.env` is not magically encrypted.** If someone gets access to the server/filesystem, they can open `.env` and see the secret.

The purpose of `.env` is mainly to **keep secrets out of your source code and Git repository**, not to make them invisible to everyone.

Let me show this using **your exact files**.

